NATIVE {"path":"/Users/kjopek/Workspace/safe-bash/tests/compatibility/bash-pipestatus-typed-native-independent-20260829/r2/HANDOFF.md","matches":[{"line":61,"text":"| P19 | 1 | `\"\"` | `\"pipestatus-typed-case: line 0: declare: PIPESTATUS: not found\\n\"` |\n| P20 | 1 | `\"\"` | `\"pipestatus-typed-case: line 0: declare: PIPESTATUS: not found\\n\"` |\n| P21 | 0 | `\"declare -ar PIPESTATUS='([0]=\\\"0\\\")'\\n\"` | `\"\"` |\n| P22 | 0 | `\"declare -- PIPESTATUS=\\\"\\\"\\ndeclare -a PIPESTATUS='([0]=\\\"0\\\")'\\n\"` | `\"\"` |\n| P23 | 0 | `\"declare -a PIPESTATUS='([0]=\\\"1\\\" [1]=\\\"0\\\")'\\ndeclare -a PIPESTATUS='([0]=\\\"0\\\")'\\n\"` | `\"\"` |\n| P24 | 0 | `\"declare -- PIPESTATUS=\\\"seed\\\"\\n\"` | `\"\"` |\n\nExact programs, without prologue or normalization:\n\n```text\nP19: declare -p PIPESTATUS\nP20: readonly PIPESTATUS; false; declare -p PIPESTATUS\nP21: false; readonly PIPESTATUS; true; declare -p PIPESTATUS\nP22: f() { local PIPESTATUS; false | true; declare -p PIPESTATUS; }; false; f; declare -p PIPESTATUS\nP23: f() { local -a PIPESTATUS; false | true; declare -p PIPESTATUS; }; false; f; declare -p PIPESTATUS\nP24: PIPESTATUS=seed; false; declare -p PIPESTATUS\n```"},{"line":62,"text":"| P20 | 1 | `\"\"` | `\"pipestatus-typed-case: line 0: declare: PIPESTATUS: not found\\n\"` |\n| P21 | 0 | `\"declare -ar PIPESTATUS='([0]=\\\"0\\\")'\\n\"` | `\"\"` |\n| P22 | 0 | `\"declare -- PIPESTATUS=\\\"\\\"\\ndeclare -a PIPESTATUS='([0]=\\\"0\\\")'\\n\"` | `\"\"` |\n| P23 | 0 | `\"declare -a PIPESTATUS='([0]=\\\"1\\\" [1]=\\\"0\\\")'\\ndeclare -a PIPESTATUS='([0]=\\\"0\\\")'\\n\"` | `\"\"` |\n| P24 | 0 | `\"declare -- PIPESTATUS=\\\"seed\\\"\\n\"` | `\"\"` |\n\nExact programs, without prologue or normalization:\n\n```text\nP19: declare -p PIPESTATUS\nP20: readonly PIPESTATUS; false; declare -p PIPESTATUS\nP21: false; readonly PIPESTATUS; true; declare -p PIPESTATUS\nP22: f() { local PIPESTATUS; false | true; declare -p PIPESTATUS; }; false; f; declare -p PIPESTATUS\nP23: f() { local -a PIPESTATUS; false | true; declare -p PIPESTATUS; }; false; f; declare -p PIPESTATUS\nP24: PIPESTATUS=seed; false; declare -p PIPESTATUS\n```\n"},{"line":71,"text":"P19: declare -p PIPESTATUS\nP20: readonly PIPESTATUS; false; declare -p PIPESTATUS\nP21: false; readonly PIPESTATUS; true; declare -p PIPESTATUS\nP22: f() { local PIPESTATUS; false | true; declare -p PIPESTATUS; }; false; f; declare -p PIPESTATUS\nP23: f() { local -a PIPESTATUS; false | true; declare -p PIPESTATUS; }; false; f; declare -p PIPESTATUS\nP24: PIPESTATUS=seed; false; declare -p PIPESTATUS\n```\n\n## Retirement, authority and native qualifications\n\nAll six case records show spawn/exit/close, null stop/signal, no errors, qualified\nclosed captures and absent-group observations. They agree with journal terminal\nrecords and final results. The journal has exactly one enrollment, terminal and\ncredit event per ID after its owner start. Per-case `receiptPublished:false`\nis the preserved pre-credit serialization state; later credit/final-results\nare checked separately. No retrospective mutation of that field occurred.\n"},{"line":72,"text":"P20: readonly PIPESTATUS; false; declare -p PIPESTATUS\nP21: false; readonly PIPESTATUS; true; declare -p PIPESTATUS\nP22: f() { local PIPESTATUS; false | true; declare -p PIPESTATUS; }; false; f; declare -p PIPESTATUS\nP23: f() { local -a PIPESTATUS; false | true; declare -p PIPESTATUS; }; false; f; declare -p PIPESTATUS\nP24: PIPESTATUS=seed; false; declare -p PIPESTATUS\n```\n\n## Retirement, authority and native qualifications\n\nAll six case records show spawn/exit/close, null stop/signal, no errors, qualified\nclosed captures and absent-group observations. They agree with journal terminal\nrecords and final results. The journal has exactly one enrollment, terminal and\ncredit event per ID after its owner start. Per-case `receiptPublished:false`\nis the preserved pre-credit serialization state; later credit/final-results\nare checked separately. No retrospective mutation of that field occurred.\n\nThe persisted ledger records **seven managed starts, peak2, active1** because"},{"line":111,"text":"| Absent with readonly marker | Preserve absence and marker; **do not force-create** | P20 does not authorize bypassing a readonly unset name |\n| Existing indexed, writable | Atomically replace the complete admitted vector | Preserve genuine stage codes and existing command-result rules |\n| Existing indexed, readonly | Recommend a narrowly internal updater exemption; retain readonly for ordinary writes | P21 proves final readonly indexed0 only, not every later transition or mutation timing |\n| Present scalar, including empty/exported scalar | Preserve value/type; no implicit scalar→array conversion | P22/P24 show local-empty and seed cases; exported behavior is a project choice |\n| Current local indexed | Update the visible local; restore the full saved outer binding/flags | P23's local1,0 then outer0 is finite evidence, not universal restoration proof |\n| Local scalar/tombstone | Honor local visibility; never fall through and update an outer hidden array | Distinguish actual absence from an existing empty scalar |\n\nNative26's P02 initial-empty display is now complemented by P19's absent\ndeclaration. Its P16 readonly-empty display is complemented by P20/P21's\ndifferent setups, not merged into one rule. P18's inner-empty/outer0 now has\ntyped local scalar/indexed counterparts. P17's post-unset visible0 remains\nfinite evidence, not an instruction to recreate every readonly absent name.\n\nThe representation supports this distinction without a new public API:\n`src/shell/arrays/bindings.ts:176` stores indexed bindings; `get():undefined`\ndoes not mean there is no scalar or readonly marker. State scalar maps,\nreadonly/exported sets and local saved/tombstone state must be consulted too."},{"line":112,"text":"| Existing indexed, writable | Atomically replace the complete admitted vector | Preserve genuine stage codes and existing command-result rules |\n| Existing indexed, readonly | Recommend a narrowly internal updater exemption; retain readonly for ordinary writes | P21 proves final readonly indexed0 only, not every later transition or mutation timing |\n| Present scalar, including empty/exported scalar | Preserve value/type; no implicit scalar→array conversion | P22/P24 show local-empty and seed cases; exported behavior is a project choice |\n| Current local indexed | Update the visible local; restore the full saved outer binding/flags | P23's local1,0 then outer0 is finite evidence, not universal restoration proof |\n| Local scalar/tombstone | Honor local visibility; never fall through and update an outer hidden array | Distinguish actual absence from an existing empty scalar |\n\nNative26's P02 initial-empty display is now complemented by P19's absent\ndeclaration. Its P16 readonly-empty display is complemented by P20/P21's\ndifferent setups, not merged into one rule. P18's inner-empty/outer0 now has\ntyped local scalar/indexed counterparts. P17's post-unset visible0 remains\nfinite evidence, not an instruction to recreate every readonly absent name.\n\nThe representation supports this distinction without a new public API:\n`src/shell/arrays/bindings.ts:176` stores indexed bindings; `get():undefined`\ndoes not mean there is no scalar or readonly marker. State scalar maps,\nreadonly/exported sets and local saved/tombstone state must be consulted too.\nFresh SOURCE-only hashing of retained accepted files matches:"}]}
